  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 28f310e05cc019a48855581da30b411e, type: 3}
  m_Name: DinuguanHistory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lines:
  - text: Stemming from pre-colonial Austronesian ritual feasting where nothing from
      the animal went to waste,
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: this rich blood stew was witnessed and recorded by foreign chroniclers
      across separate centuries,
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: including Antonio Pigafetta in 1521, Miguel de Loarca in 1582, and Francisco
      Ignacio Alcina in 1668.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Can you balance the vinegar and aromatics to earn its traditional place
      on your table?
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
